# SiteLaunch Marketing Cockpit, environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. Leave everything blank to run in local mode, which
# stores data in the browser and needs no account. That is the default.
#
# ONE RULE, AND IT IS ABSOLUTE
#
# Anything named VITE_ is inlined into the JavaScript at build time and is readable
# by anyone who opens the browser developer tools. Only put values here that are
# designed to be public. Every secret belongs in the server side secret store,
# never in this file. See server/README.md.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser safe. These two are the only variables the app itself reads.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Supabase project URL, for example https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The Supabase ANON key, also called the publishable key.
# Safe in the browser by design. It grants nothing on its own, because row level
# security decides what the signed in user can read. Never put the service role
# key here: it bypasses row level security entirely.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER SIDE ONLY. Names listed so the next sprint knows what to provision.
# None of these are read by this app, and none may ever be prefixed with VITE_.
# They belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets or Supabase Vault.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase service role key. Bypasses row level security, so a sync using it must
# set owner_id explicitly on every row it writes.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Google OAuth, shared by GA4, Search Console and Calendar.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=

# Google Analytics 4.
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=

# Google Search Console. The verified property, for example https://sitelaunchstudios.com/
# SEARCH_CONSOLE_SITE_URL=

# Google Calendar. Which calendar tasks are written to.
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=

# Meta, covering both Instagram and Facebook.
# META_APP_ID=
# META_APP_SECRET=
# META_SYSTEM_USER_TOKEN=
# INSTAGRAM_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID=
# FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID=

# LinkedIn, later.
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Shared secret the website posts enquiries with, so the endpoint can tell a real
# submission from anyone who found the URL.
# WEBSITE_FORM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
